## Essential Rules
- Correctness > Readability > Performance > DX > Maintainability
- Explicit, clear code; no `any`.
- Prettier formatting, strict TypeScript.
- Light/dark theme support.

### Packages
- Always use `npx expo install <package>` (never npm/yarn/pnpm) for dependencies.

### TypeScript
- Strict mode, no `any`.
- Components: PascalCase. Hooks: `use*`.
- Imports order: External → Internal → Types → Constants.
- Use ThemedText/ThemedView.

### Auth Tokens
- Save to secure storage before updating state.
- Use `saveAuthData(session, user)` from `lib/secure-storage.ts`.

### Testing
- `"test": "jest"` (never watch mode by default).
- Mock external dependencies.
- Use `waitFor(..., { timeout: 3000 })`.
- Await all promises.
- Cleanup in `afterEach`.
- Test business logic only.
- See `prevent-hanging-tests.mdc`.

### Code Quality
- No console.log (except errors).
- Handle loading, success, error states.
- Never mutate state directly.

## Stack
- Expo Router, Zustand, Supabase, NativeWind, OTP+Biometric only.

## Architecture
- Folders: `app/`, `components/`, `stores/`, `lib/`, `hooks/`, `utils/`.
- State: Zustand for global, useState for local.
- Style: NativeWind (prefer className).
- Auth: OTP+Biometric in `stores/use-auth-store.ts`.

## Security
- Use `expo-secure-store` for sensitive data.
- Supabase RLS always enabled.
- Never expose service role keys.